    "note": "The MCP input schema is z.object({ connectionId }).strict() (src/configuration-bte-metadata.ts:13-15), so connectionId is the ONLY input; there is no product, table or view parameter to set. The first thing the handler does is resolve the client (tools.ts:6860) and require client 200, then attest the DEPLOYED helper: sourceFingerprint, interfaceFingerprint, remoteEnabled true, updateTask false, globalInterface false, and importParameters / changingParameters / exceptions all EMPTY (src/configuration-bte-metadata.ts:38-68). What a refusal would mean, MEASURED locally on 2026-10-15 rather than assumed: the interface fingerprint b498f6e9... is identical in r74 postdeploy and r75 sourceRepair and importParameters is [] in both, while only the SOURCE fingerprint moved - 2a7ee180... (r74) to 8fe403c4... (r75 repair). The declared pin 8fe403c4... is therefore the r75 repaired body, although the comment at src/configuration-bte-metadata-api.ts:1 still says 'w200 r74'; that provenance claim is inaccurate and is checked by no assertion. GRANTED_ACTVT was never an import parameter of Z_ORVANTA_CFG_BTE_META: in the r75 evidence it appears only inside the ABAP source body as the lowercase `granted_actvt = lv_granted` clause of the standard CALL FUNCTION 'VIEW_AUTHORITY_CHECK', which the r75 repair DELETED along with the lv_granted declaration, so the surviving copies are only in the oldString being replaced. Consequently BTE_METADATA_API_UNVERIFIED here means the live deployed source or interface has DRIFTED from the declared r75 pin - the genuinely open question - and NOT that an optional GRANTED_ACTVT parameter is present. Record it, stop, never retry it, never relax the attestation to admit the live values. BTE_METADATA_LAYOUT_UNVERIFIED or BTE_METADATA_STANDARD_API_UNVERIFIED mean the VIMDESC/VIMNAMTAB/TVIMF layout or the pinned SVIX standard API has moved. Success is status 'native_metadata_read' with EV_CODE METADATA_READ_OK."
